[18.97,"o","\u001b[2K\u001b[G\u001b[32m?\u001b[39m \u001b[1mUse existing SAP AI Core configuration?\u001b[22m\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mYes\u001b[39m\u001b[45D\u001b[45C\r\n\r\n🔄 Using existing configuration from gateway .env file\r\n\r\nGenerating Kubernetes manifests...\r\n\r\n✅ namespace.yaml created\r\n✅ Image pull secret template created as registry-secret.yaml.template (requires manual configuration)\r\n✅ Secret manifests created\r\n🔧 Generating Dex configuration for local provider...\r\n✅ Loaded Docker config from docker/configs/providers/local/dex.config.yaml\r\n✅ Using Docker-generated static passwords for local provider\r\n✅ Dex configuration generated successfully\r\n✅ ConfigMap manifests created\r\n📝 Processing core service manifests from templates...\r\n   useDigests: false\r\n   imageDigests: 0 digests\r\n📝 Processing postgres.yaml from template...\r\n✅ postgres.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing valkey.yaml from template...\r\n✅ valkey.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing gateway.yaml from template...\r\n✅ gateway.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing admin.yaml from template...\r\n✅ admin.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing nginx.yaml from template...\r\n✅ nginx.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ Core service manifests processed from templates\r\n📝 Processing auth service manifests from templates...\r\n📝 Processing oauth2-proxy.yaml from template...\r\n✅ OAuth2-proxy configured with hybrid endpoints:\r\n   External login: https://sail.example.com/dex/auth\r\n   External callback: https://sail.example.com/oauth2/callback\r\n   Internal token/JWKS: http://dex:5556/dex/*\r\n   OIDC discovery: disabled (avoids startup circular dependency)\r\n✅ oauth2-proxy.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing dex.yaml from template...\r\n"]
[19.423,"o","✅ Dex API access pinned to kubernetes.default ClusterIP 203.0.113.7 (Gardener 421 workaround)\r\n✅ dex.yaml generated from template\r\n📝 Processing dex-rbac.yaml from template...\r\n✅ dex-rbac.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ Auth service manifests processed from templates\r\n📝 Processing networking manifests from templates...\r\n✅ apirule-examples.yaml generated from template\r\n🗑️  Removed apirule-examples.yaml - streaming VirtualService will handle all traffic\r\n✅ apirule.yaml generated from template\r\n🗑️  Removed apirule.yaml - streaming VirtualService will handle all traffic\r\n✅ destination-rules.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ health-check-protection.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ peer-authentication.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ streaming-envoyfilter.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ streaming-virtualservice.yaml generated from template\r\n✅ <redacted>.yaml created with IP allowlist: 203.0.113.7/32\r\n✅ <redacted>.yaml created for SCC tunnel (sail.example.com)\r\n✅ Networking manifests processed from templates\r\n🔒 Local .env and docker configuration backed up to /tmp/sail-proxy-local-config-jEqlgk\r\n   (restored automatically when setup finishes; copy back from there if setup is killed)\r\n   Moved aside services/gateway/.env (restored when setup finishes)\r\n   Moved aside services/admin/.env (restored when setup finishes)\r\n   Moved aside services/ollama/.env (restored when setup finishes)\r\n\r\n🔧 Preparing Docker configuration for nginx build...\r\n   Running: node docker/setup-docker.js --config <configuration>\r\n📋 Using configuration from --config parameter\r\n"]
[19.583,"o","\r\n============================================================\r\n   SAIL-PROXY Docker Setup (Configuration Mode)\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n\r\nChecking service configuration files...\r\n\r\n📝 Creating Gateway .env file...\r\n✅ Gateway .env created successfully\r\n\r\n🔒 SECURITY WARNING: SAP AI Core credentials stored in .env file\r\n   For production deployments, consider using:\r\n   - OS environment variables (export CLIENT_SECRET=xxx)\r\n   - Docker secrets or Kubernetes secrets\r\n   - External secret management (HashiCorp Vault, etc.)\r\n   - Set file permissions: chmod 600 services/gateway/.env\r\n📝 Creating Admin .env file...\r\n✅ Admin .env created successfully\r\n📝 Creating Ollama .env file...\r\n✅ Ollama .env created successfully\r\n\r\n🔐 Validating shared security tokens...\r\n\r\n✅ VALIDATION_TOKEN_SECRET matches\r\n✅ METADATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY matches\r\n\r\n✅ All security tokens validated successfully\r\n📋 Skipping backup in configuration mode\r\n\r\nCopying and configuring files...\r\nℹ️  Nginx configuration is now handled via environment variables\r\n   See docker/nginx/README.md for details\r\n✅ .env.postgres configured\r\n✅ .env.filesearch-runtime configured\r\n✅ .env.nginx created with BASE_URL=https://sail.example.com\r\n✅ Database credentials written to docker/.env (POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD)\r\n✅ dex.config.yaml updated with database credentials\r\n✅ dex.config.yaml configured\r\n✅ .env.auth configured\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\n   Setup Complete! 🎉\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n✅ Configured for: Local Development (hardcoded users)\r\n✅ Base URL: https://sail.example.com\r\n"]
[19.692,"o","\r\nGenerated/Updated files:\r\n  Service Configuration:\r\n  - services/gateway/.env (SAP AI Core configuration)\r\n  - services/admin/.env (Admin service configuration)\r\n  - services/ollama/.env (Ollama service configuration)\r\n  Authentication Configuration:\r\n  - .env.nginx (Nginx environment variables)\r\n  - dex.config.yaml (with provider-specific configuration)\r\n  - .env.auth (updated OAuth2 URLs)\r\n  - .env.postgres (PostgreSQL configuration for Docker)\r\n\r\n💡 Configuration verification:\r\n   node verify-config.js\r\n\r\n✅ Nginx uses environment variables for configuration!\r\n   No rebuild required - configuration is applied at container startup.\r\n   The nginx image can be built once and reused across environments.\r\n\r\n🍎 Apple Silicon (ARM64) Detected\r\n   All services support native ARM64 for optimal performance.\r\n\r\nfailed to connect to the docker API at unix:///var/run/docker.sock; check if the path is correct and if the daemon is running: dial unix /var/run/docker.sock: connect: no such file or directory\r\nNext steps:\r\n1. Build containers (only needed once):\r\n   docker-compose build\r\n\r\n   Note: Future configuration changes only require container restart.\r\n\r\n2. Start the services:\r\n   docker-compose up -d\r\n\r\n3. Access the application:\r\n   https://sail.example.com/admin/\r\n\r\n💡 Apple Silicon Notes:\r\n   • All images are now multi-architecture (ARM64 and AMD64)\r\n   • Native ARM64 performance for optimal speed\r\n   • No platform-specific overrides needed\r\n\r\n4. Test users:\r\n   - admin@example.com / admin123\r\n   - user@example.com / user123\r\n\r\n🔑 Generated Credentials:\r\n   Save these credentials for future access:\r\n\r\n   📊 Database Credentials:\r\n   - Username: admin_user\r\n   - Password: [Set via Kyma configuration]\r\n\r\n   🔐 OAuth2 Proxy Secrets:\r\n   - Client Secret: ••••••••\r\n   - Cookie Secret: ••••••••\r\n\r\n   These credentials are stored in your .env files and used by the services.\r\n   The database password is randomized for security.\r\n\r\n🔒 Security Reminders:\r\n   - Review .env files for sensitive data before committing to git\r\n   - Use OS environment variables for production secrets\r\n   - Set restrictive file permissions: chmod 600 services/*/.env\r\n   - Consider external secret management for enterprise deployments\r\n\r\nFor troubleshooting, check the logs:\r\n   docker-compose logs\r\n\r\n✅ Docker setup completed successfully\r\n   Using matching configuration from Kyma setup\r\n   The nginx image will work with both Docker and Kyma deployments\r\n\r\n📋 Post-processing environment files for Kyma deployment...\r\n\r\n📝 Creating environment ConfigMaps...\r\n✅ gateway-config.yaml created\r\n✅ admin-config.yaml created\r\n📝 Creating api_config.json ConfigMap...\r\n✅ admin-api-config.yaml created\r\n📝 Updating deployment manifests to use ConfigMaps...\r\n✅ admin.yaml already has ConfigMap references, skipping update\r\n✅ Post-processing completed successfully\r\n🔒 Restored local configuration: services/gateway/.env, services/admin/.env, docker/.env, docker/.env.postgres, docker/.env.filesearch-runtime, docker/.env.nginx, docker/.env.auth, docker/dex.config.yaml\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\n   Setup Complete! 🎉\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n✅ Configured for: Local Development (hardcoded users)\r\n✅ Deployment Type: Public HTTPS\r\n✅ Container Registry: ghcr.io/st-gr/sail-proxy-private\r\n✅ Image Version: docs-800da807\r\n✅ Domain: sail-proxy-test\r\n✅ IP Allowlist: 203.0.113.7/32\r\n\r\n🔑 Generated Credentials:\r\n   Save these credentials for future access:\r\n\r\n   📊 Database Credentials:\r\n   - Username: admin_user\r\n   - Password: ••••••••\r\n\r\n   🔐 Security Secrets:\r\n   - Validation Token: ••••••••\r\n   - Metadata Encryption Key: <redacted>\r\n   - AWS Secret Encryption Key: ••••••••\r\n   - OAuth2 Client Secret: ••••••••\r\n   - OAuth2 Cookie Secret: ••••••••\r\n\r\n   These credentials are stored in Kubernetes Secrets and used by the services.\r\n   All secrets are randomly generated for maximum security.\r\n\r\nGenerated files:\r\n  Kubernetes Manifests:\r\n  - manifests/core/namespace.yaml\r\n  - templates/secrets/*.yaml (PostgreSQL, Gateway, Admin, OAuth2-Proxy secrets)\r\n  - templates/secrets/registry-secret.yaml.template (Manual creation required)\r\n  - templates/configmaps/*.yaml (NGINX, Dex, Gateway, Admin, API configs)\r\n  - manifests/core/*.yaml (Service deployments with ConfigMap integration)\r\n  - manifests/networking/*.yaml (APIRule, AuthorizationPolicy)\r\n\r\n💡 Next steps:\r\n1. Build and push Docker images:\r\n   # From project root\r\n   docker build -t ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807 -f docker/gateway.Dockerfile .\r\n   docker build -t ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807 -f docker/admin.Dockerfile .\r\n   docker build -t ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807 -f docker/nginx/Dockerfile docker\r\n   \r\n   docker push ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807\r\n   docker push ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807\r\n   docker push ghcr.<redacted>:docs-800da807\r\n\r\n2. Deploy to Kyma:\r\n   # Windows PowerShell:\r\n   $env:KYMA_DEPLOY_CONFIG=\"<redacted>\"; node kyma/scripts/deploy-kyma.js --namespace sail-proxy-test; Remove-Item Env:\\KYMA_DEPLOY_CONFIG\r\n\r\n   # Linux/Mac:\r\n   KYMA_DEPLOY_CONFIG=\"<redacted>\" node kyma/scripts/deploy-kyma.js --namespace sail-proxy-test\r\n\r\n\r\n📝 Manual steps (if needed):\r\n\r\n🌐 Your application will be available at:\r\n   Gateway API: https://sail.example.com/gateway\r\n   Admin OData: https://sail.example.com/admin/odata/v4/admin\r\n   Adm.Cockpit: https://sail.example.com/admin/app/shell/\r\n\r\n🔒 Security Notes:\r\n   - Secrets are stored in Kubernetes Secret objects\r\n   - ConfigMaps contain non-sensitive configuration only\r\n   - IP allowlisting is configured via Istio AuthorizationPolicy in istio-system namespace\r\n   - Images use public GitHub container registry (ghcr.io/st-gr/sail-proxy-*)\r\n\r\n\u001b[?25h$ "]
